# ubuntu-genesis repository

This repo is a **Quarto website** of installation guides (Ubuntu, software,
Git, R packages, LaTeX). It is not the DeCovarT package.

## Layout

- Pages at the root (`index.qmd`, `ubuntu.qmd`, `software.qmd`, `network.qmd`,
  `onedrive.qmd`, `r.qmd`, `git.qmd`, `latex.qmd`) and `_quarto.yml`.
- `assets/` — figures, scripts, and PDFs, one subfolder per topic.
- `Config/` — portable dotfiles and **Cursor bundle** (`Config/.cursor/rules/`,
  `Config/.cursor/skills/`). Students copy or symlink into `~/.cursor/`.
- Rendered HTML goes to `docs/` and is published by GitHub Actions, not
  committed.

## Conventions

- British English in prose; reproducible Quarto where chunks run.
- Cross-link pages from `index.qmd`; keep `_quarto.yml` `project.render`
  and the navbar in sync when adding pages.
- LaTeX page aligns with `latex.qmd` and `rules/latex-scientific.mdc`.
- Do not commit secrets, API keys, or machine-specific paths in shared Config.

## Deploying Cursor rules from this bundle

```bash
# user-wide (recommended for teaching defaults)
cp -r Config/.cursor/rules/* ~/.cursor/rules/
cp -r Config/.cursor/skills/* ~/.cursor/skills/

# or per-project
mkdir -p .cursor/rules .cursor/skills
cp -r Config/.cursor/rules/* .cursor/rules/
cp -r Config/.cursor/skills/* .cursor/skills/
```

Install Firecrawl skills separately (see `skills/firecrawl/SKILL.md`).
